    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Good morning and welcome to Hudson Institute. I'm Ken Weinstein, Japan Chair here at Hudson, delighted to welcome Congressman Andy Kim of the Third District of New Jersey to today's event, preserving a free and open Indo-Pacific. The Congressman is finishing his third term in the House of Representatives. He is the first Korean-American Democratic member of the House of Representatives. And if the polls hold as they currently do, this November, he is very likely to be the first Korean-American Democratic member of the U.S. Senate. He is a bit of an unusual background for a member of Congress. He served previously at USAID, the Pentagon, the State Department, and the NSC, as well as in Afghanistan before his election. Now, we share an important bond. We were both students of Nathan Tarkoff at the University of Chicago, and Congressman Kim went on to do a PhD at Maudland College Oxford as a Rhodes Scholar, doing PhD in International Relations, and he is using that his PhD studies well, I can say. I was just at my 40th reunion of the time when I began my PhD program, and everybody else was in academia where I was, so",
