    "turn_text": "different. But currently serves in the House Foreign Affairs Committee, notably on the Indo-Pacific subcommittee. We had the honor of, as well, of having Congresswoman Young Kim, who chairs that committee a few months back. And the chairman, the congressman also serves on the House Armed Services Committee, as well as on the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party. So let me begin first by sort of focusing a bit on your background. It's a little unusual for a member of Congress to have had so much time in so many different federal departments before being elected, and particularly in Afghanistan, where you were an advisor to both General Petraeus and General Allen. And on the NSC, you obviously focus on the fight against ISIS under President Obama.",
