    "turn_text": "there. It's clear we need more naval assets for deterrence in the Indo-Pacific and arguably also in the Mediterranean. Given the concerns about capacity and capability of US shipyards, do you worry about the weakening of the US naval industry? One of the interesting things we've now seen is Hanwah, the Korean shipping companies now investing in Philadelphia, Navy Yard, which was obviously played a critical role in World War II and since, but it's since fallen on hard times. What actions do you think the US and its allies should do to improve our capabilities, and in particular, are you as naval industry?",
